    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15380" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρουρ-αῖος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰρ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>from the
				country, rural, rustic,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῦς ἀ.</span>
			<i>field</i>-vole, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.141
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμίνθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					227
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ παῖ τῆς ἀ. θεοῦ,</span> of
			Euripides as the reputed son of a <i>herb</i>-seller, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				840
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. Οἰνόμαος,</span> of
			Aeschines, who played the part of Oenomaüs 'in the
			provinces', <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.242
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				211
			</span></i> sq.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. λίθοι</span>
			<i>rough</i> stones, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				2587.21
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυτὰ ἀ.</span>
			<i>field</i>-weeds, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				7.6.1
			</span></i>.</div>
